      "problem": "Evaluate $z=\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}$ at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
